    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Dad, are you happy today?” My younger daughter asked me as I picked her up from school on March 20."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Am I happy?” I tried to answer her question. “Why are you asking this?”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Today is the International Day of Happiness,” she replied. “It’s a day to be happy!”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“So did you have a happy day?”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Of course! I learned how to draw a picture of bamboo today.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Good,” I said. “If you are happy, then I am, too.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "My daughter nodded with a smile. She seemed happy about my answer. But the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "conversation",
            "ref": "v-conversation"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " made me "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "think deeply about",
            "ref": "v-think-deeply-about"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " happiness."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What is happiness? How can I get it? It’s hard to answer these two questions. Maybe I should feel happy when my wife "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "praises",
            "ref": "v-praise"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " my cooking. But I know she’s very kind. I know I’m not really a good cook. The more I think this way, the less happy I feel. Maybe I should feel happy whenever my daughters tell me that they had a good day at school. But when they think I’m interested in their day; they’ll talk and talk about it. Then, I often have to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "stay up late",
            "ref": "v-stay-up-late"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to write my articles. I’ll feel tired—and unhappy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p9",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "My daughters don’t think so much about happiness. And they seem to be happy on most days. They are happy when their teachers praise them. They are happy when I take them to the zoo (they love animals)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p10",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Perhaps I can learn something from my daughters (and from you, too) about how to be happy. Perhaps I’ll feel happier if I stop thinking too much about happiness."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
